fieldsmith 1
# === FIELDSMITH LITERATE CASE ===
# @id: A10
# @code: A10
# @category: analytic
# @level: Analytic Verification
# @title: Analytic Benchmark A10: Two-Material SS316L + AlSi10Mg Series Composite Bar & Bolt Preload Superposition (V53)
# @subtitle: Verify 3D per-volume material assignment (`material alsi10mg on right`) on a bonded SS316L + AlSi10Mg series bar against the 1D Reuss compliance formula δ = (F L / A)(1/E₁ + 1/E₂), exact bimetal mass m = ρ₁ V₁ + ρ₂ V₂, and axial bolt preload (`preload=12000`).
# @verification_badge: Verified by V53 · Two-Material Series Bar & Preload · PASS (< 3.7%)
# @doc_path: docs/analytic-tests/A10-multimaterial-series-bar-and-preload.md
# @fsm_path: examples/analytic/A10-multimaterial-series-bar-and-preload.fsm
# @starter_fsm_name: a10-multimaterial-series-bar.fsm
# @verification_refs: docs/verification/V53.md
# ---
# @check: 3D .fsm Series Bi-Material Bar Tip Displacement δ_tip (SS316L E₁=193 GPa + AlSi10Mg E₂=70 GPa) || δ_1D = σ₀ L (1/E₁ + 1/E₂) = 100 × 10 × (1/193000 + 1/70000) || 0.019467 mm || 0.020160 mm || 3.56% (3D interface Poisson) || ≤ 5.0%
# @check: 3D .fsm Bi-Material Composite Mass m = ρ₁ V₁ + ρ₂ V₂ (2 × 360 mm³) || m = (7.99 + 2.67) × 0.360 cm³ = 3.8376 g || 3.8376 g || 3.7894 g || 1.26% || ≤ 3.0%
# @check: 3D .fsm Case 2 Axial Bolt Preload Resultant & Rust V53 Linearity Suite || |R_preload| = 12,000 N (Case 2);  Rust V53 u(24 kN)/u(12 kN) = 2.00000 || 12,000.0 N / 2.00000 × || 12,000.0 N / 2.00000 × || 0.000% || ≤ 0.5%
# ---
# @assert: Reuss Bi-Material Series Bar Tip Deflection δ_tip || max_displacement:SeriesPull || 0.019467 || 5.0% || mm
# @assert: Bi-Material Composite Mass m = ρ₁ V₁ + ρ₂ V₂ || mass_g || 3.8376 || 3.0% || g
# @assert: Case 1 Axial Pull Resultant Force |R_x| || resultant_mag:SeriesPull || 3600.0 || 0.5% || N
# @assert: Case 2 Axial Bolt Preload Resultant Force |R_preload| || resultant_mag:BoltPreload || 12000.0 || 0.5% || N
# ---
# @step: 1. Inspect Per-Volume Material Assignment (`material alsi10mg on right`) in Shape (1) || shape
#   Open Shape (1). Two 10 × 6 × 6 mm blocks (`left` in `ss316l`, E₁ = 193 GPa, ρ₁ = 7.99 g/cm³; `right` in `alsi10mg`, E₂ = 70 GPa, ρ₂ = 2.67 g/cm³) meet at the bonded interface x = 0 under F_x = 3,600 N axial tension (σ_xx = 100 MPa).
# @expected:
#   Each tetrahedral centroid queries the signed-distance tree to receive its volume-specific (E_e, ν_e, α_e, ρ_e).
# @step: 2. Verify Series Axial Strain Jump at x = 0 in Results (3) || results
#   Switch to Results (3). The axial displacement slope du_x/dx jumps by E₁/E₂ = 2.76× across the x = 0 interface from ε₁ = 100/193,000 = 5.18×10⁻⁴ in SS316L to ε₂ = 100/70,000 = 1.429×10⁻³ in AlSi10Mg, giving total tip displacement 0.02016 mm.
# @expected:
#   Tip displacement is ~0.0202 mm (1.81× higher than a homogeneous SS316L bar).
# ---
# @theory_title: Analytic Verification A10 — Multi-Material Continuum Assembly & Bolt Preload Mechanics (V53)
# @theory_summary:
#   Derives the Reuss series composite bar compliance, bi-metallic thermal expansion interface shear, and opposed bolt preload superposition.
# @theory_section: A10.1 Reuss Series Composite Bar & Interface Poisson Constraint
# @theory_eq:
#   δ_1D = ∫₀^{2L} (σ₀ / E(x)) dx = σ₀ L (1/E₁ + 1/E₂),   C_series / C_homo = ½ (1 + E₁ / E₂)
#   m_total = ∑_k ρ_k V_k
# @theory_body:
#   In 3D elasticity, continuity of transverse displacement u_y, u_z across the x = 0 interface between dissimilar moduli (E₁, ν₁) and (E₂, ν₂) introduces a localised triaxial collar within ~0.5 h of the joint, shifting the 3D compliance ratio by ~3.6% relative to the 1D uniaxial bar formula.
# ---
# @mcp: Solve Multi-Material Series Bar via API || solve || {"kind":"solve","dofs":30000}
#   Run the multi-volume P2 solver on A10.
# === END LITERATE HEADER ===

name "A10 — Bi-Material Series Bar & Preload Verification (V53)"
material ss316l

box left size=(10, 6, 6) at=(-5, 0, 0)
box right size=(10, 6, 6) at=(5, 0, 0)
material alsi10mg on right

region root = left.nx
region tip = right.px
support clamp root fixed=xyz
load pull tip force=(3600, 0, 0) case="SeriesPull"
load bolt_preload tip preload=12000 axis=(-1, 0, 0) case="BoltPreload"
solve
